MatchedObjectDescriptor.QualificationSummary:
GS-05: Your resume must demonstrate at least one year of specialized experience at or equivalent to the GS-04 grade level or pay band in the Federal service or equivalent experience in the private or public sector. Specialized experience must demonstrate the following: performing technical support processing personnel actions, preparing reports, and maintaining records in an automated recruitment system;
OR
Have successfully completed four years of education above high school level in any field for which high school graduation or the equivalent is the normal prerequisite;
OR
Have a combination of specialized experience and education that equates to one year of experience. The percentage of the required experience plus the percentage of the required education must equal one hundred percent. GS-04: Your resume must demonstrate at least one year of general experience in the Federal service or equivalent experience in the private or public sector. General experience must demonstrate the following: progressively responsible clerical, office, or other work that indicates ability to acquire the particular knowledge and skills needed to perform the duties of the position to be filled;
OR
Have successfully completed two years of education above high school level in any field for which high school graduation or the equivalent is the normal prerequisite.
OR
Have a combination of general experience and education that equates to one year of experience. The percentage of the required experience plus the percentage of the required education must equal one hundred percent. Additional qualification information can be found from the following Office of Personnel Management web site: https://www.opm.gov/policy-data-oversight/classification-qualifications/general-schedule-qualification-standards/#url=GS-CLER. Experience refers to paid and unpaid experience, including volunteer work done through National Service programs (e.g., professional, philanthropic, religious, spiritual, community, student, social). Volunteer work helps build critical competencies, knowledge, and skills and can provide valuable training and experience that translates directly to paid employment.

GS-12:
Your resume must demonstrate at least one year of specialized experience at or equivalent to the GS-11 grade level or pay band in the Federal service or equivalent experience in the private or public sector. Specialized experience must demonstrate the following: 1) Providing an organization with federal civilian human resources advisory services for staffing, classification, position management, and compensation;
2) Providing internal and external services to an organization for recruiting highly specialized and hard-to-fill federal civilian positions; and
3) Analyzing and advising on the concepts, principles, laws, policies, rules, regulations, precedents, and procedures for performing federal civilian classification and position management. NOTE: This experience must be fully supported by the information in your resume. GS-11:
Your resume must demonstrate at least one year of specialized experience at or equivalent to the GS-09 grade level or pay band in the Federal service or equivalent experience in the private or public sector. Specialized experience must demonstrate the following: 1) Assisting an organization in meeting its federal civilian staffing, classification, position management, and compensation needs;
2) Reviewing and analyzing position descriptions utilizing federal classification standards;
3) Applying position management principles and techniques to provide management advisory services regarding organizational structures and career development; and
4) Resolving problems, answering questions, and providing guidance on complex staffing and position classification problems utilizing human resources tools and systems. NOTE: This experience must be fully supported by the information in your resume. Additional qualification information can be found from the following Office of Personnel Management web site: https://www.opm.gov/policy-data-oversight/classification-qualifications/general-schedule-qualification-standards/#url=List-by-Occupational-Series Experience refers to paid and unpaid experience, including volunteer work done through National Service programs (e.g., professional, philanthropic, religious, spiritual, community, student, social). Volunteer work helps build critical competencies, knowledge, and skills and can provide valuable training and experience that translates directly to paid employment.
